1	Objective and Scope
This document describes the business requirements  for the TechMarket Project. It contains the overall description of the application, the scope of data migration, and any changes need to be performed during migration of the application.
This document along with the prototype demo is used for requirements confirmation, and it is to be signed off by the business. Details of business logic and graphic user interface of the application, which are not mentioned in this document, will be migrated as they are in the application.
2	Business Requirement
2.1.	Application Overview
TechMarket is a used electronics classifieds website. It allows users to post complete information about the item they want to sell, then buyers can consider purchasing.
Administrators can manage user accounts. If a user has a low rating and is reported for trading behavior, the Administrator may consider banning this account. Administrators can review and delete posts that violate business regulations and policies.
Sellers can post posts to sell items including basic information about the item. This post must be reviewed by an administrator to ensure that its information is valid and truthful. Once the post is approved, it will be viewed by everyone who visits the website. A collection of posts managed by the seller themselves with different statuses. TechMarket provides a 'payment guarantee' feature for posts so that buyers can create orders and transfer money to TechMarket's account as a form of intermediary holding money, which will be paid to the seller when The transaction is confirmed by the buyer.
TechMarket offers another interesting feature called 'push post', by using this feature, sellers can push their post to the front page so that it is easily seen by buyers, increasing the likelihood of a sale. .
Buyers can search for desired products on the website and make purchases in two ways. Method 1, text and exchange with the seller to agree on the receiving address, payment method, delivery method,... . Method 2, use the ordering feature for posts that apply 'guarantee payment' to ensure your money is kept safe before receiving the goods. Buyers can also report violative posts.
In addition, users can access the help center to see how to use the website's features and can also send feedback to improve the website.
The Customer Care Department can manage the help center page and process user feedback.




2.2.	Domain Model
2.2.1.	Diagram 








2.2.2.	Domain Objects Description
#	Object Name	Object Description
1	Admin	Users in this group have permission to manage user accounts, posts, legal documents, categories.
2	User	Users in this group have permission to place order, manage their own posts, leave a feedback
3	Customer Care Department	Users in this group have permission to view and handle feedback from all users.
4	Legal document	The object contains the information of legal documents.
5	Category	The object contains the information of categories
6	Post	The object contains the post’s information.
7	Order	The object contains the order’s information, created by the system when the user makes a purchase.
8	Bill	The object contains the information of the order, buyer, seller and other needed information
9	Payment Method	The object contains the information of payment method.
10	Product	The object contains the information of product, just create when user creates a post.
11	Address	The object contains the information of the shipping address.
12	Post push service	The object contains the information of the post push service.
13	Feedback	The object contains the information of feedback
14	Help center	The object contains the information of help center



2.3.	Workflow
2.4.	Use Cases and Actors
2.4.1.	Diagram


2.4.2.	Description of Actors
#	Actor Name	Definition
1	Admin	Administrator of the whole system, is responsible for order management and post management. Admin makes sure that posts and orders are valid.
2	User	Who registers with the system
3	Buyer	Users who want to sell their used electronic device
4	Seller	Users who want to buy electronic devices
5	Customer care department	Users who handle customer feedback and provide documents to the help center



2.4.3.	Description of Use Cases
#	Use Case Name	Definition
1	Sign In	This use case describes the process by which a user logs into the system.
2	Sign Up	This use case describes the process by which a user creates a new account in the system.
3	Forgot password	This use case describes how user can 
4	Leave a feedback	This use case describes how user can leave a feedback 
5	Create post	This use case descibes how user can create a post for selling electronic devices
6	Update post	This use case describes how user can update a post
7	Delete post	This use case describes how user can delete a post
8	Guarantee payment	This use case describes how users can use guaranteed payment functionality for their posts
9	Link sales wallet	This use case describes how a user can link to their merchant wallet
10	Use post push service	This use case describes how a user can use the post push service, increase product sales.
11	Confirm sales order	This use case describes how sellers can confirm the order of buyers.
12	Place order	This use case describes how user can place an order for product they want to buy
13	Choose shipping address	This use case describes how a user can select an existing address or create a new one
14	Pay 	This use case describes how users can pay for their payment
15	Cancel order	This use case describes how a user can cancel an order
16	Confirm delivery of order	This use case describes how buyer can confirm that they receive product 
17	Rate seller	This use case describes how buyer can rate the seller after receiving order
18	Chat with seller	This use case describes how user can contact with seller for finding out more about the product 
19	Report post	This use case describes how users can report violative posts
20	Create category	This use case describes how users can create new categories for the system
21	Update category name	This use case describes how a user can change the category information
22	Delete category	This use case describes how a user can delete a category
23	Approve post	This use case describes how admin can approve a post to makes it visible on user’s wall
24	Reject post	This use case describes how admin can reject a post due to the policy
25	Ban account	This use case describes how a user can ban a user account that violates website’s regulations
26	Manage TechMarket bank account	This use case describes how a user can manage a client's trading currency storage account
27	Update legal documents	This use case describes how users can update legal documents related to a publicly available website
28	Update information for the help center	This use case describes how users can update content and questions for the help center
29	Handle feedback from user	This use case describes how users can view and respond to customer feedback





